      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART V, LINE 4:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION MAINTAINS 21 NAMED ENDOWED SCHOLARSHIPS FUNDS. FOLLOWING THE CREATION OF EACH FUND, SCHOLARSHIPS, GRANTS, AND/OR AWARDS ARE DISBURSED FROM THE EARNINGS ON THE ENDOWED GIFTS AND IN KEEPING WITH THE DONOR'S DESIGNATIONS. IN MAY 2008, THE CALIFORNIA COMMUNITY COLLEGES SCHOLARSHIP (CCCS) ENDOWMENT WAS LAUNCHED VIA A GIFT OF $25 MILLION FROM THE BERNARD OSHER FOUNDATION TO THE FOUNDATION FOR CALIFORNIA COMMUNITY COLLEGES (FCCC). THE PURPOSE OF THE CCCS ENDOWMENT IS TO PROVIDE SCHOLARSHIPS FOR STUDENTS IN CALIFORNIA'S COMMUNITY COLLEGE SYSTEM.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleD>
